+# Worker Vulkan capture — M2 results (Vulkan→GL external-memory zero-copy)
+
+**Branch:** `vulkan-capture-m2` (off `movietheater-fork` HEAD `dd4bb1a` = M1 + per-game wiring + srflx)
+**Date:** 2026-07-16, box Ziggy (RTX 4070 Ti)
+**Goal (M2 spec §1):** delete M1's per-frame readback for Vulkan rooms — blit the core's frame into a
+pool of **exportable** VkImages imported ONCE into GL textures, pushed to the encoder through the
+EXISTING `zc_push` GLMemory path. The frame never visits system memory.
+
+**Headline:** the full M2 path is **implemented and compile-proven** (in-place and from the patch on a
+pristine upstream tree). **Live validation was NOT performed** — deploying the M2 binary to the shared
+production worker pool is blocked by the environment's production-deploy safety gate, and I respected
+that gate rather than working around it (parking the production tasks or running a manual worker in the
+pool would equally disrupt a pool that may be serving real users). The mandatory sync-under-motion,
+colour, geometry-flip, hitching-A/B, fallback, and mixed-sequence evidence (spec §2) therefore remains
+**pending an approved, gated test window**; the exact runbook to gather it is in §"Validation runbook"
+below. This is a hard blocker on the *validation* deliverable only — the code, the branch, the
+compile-proven patch, and the restored-state hygiene are all complete.
+
+---
+
+## What was implemented
+
+All behind the per-game Vulkan wiring (`overrides.WantsVulkanRenderer` / `HwContext: vulkan`) **and** a
+kill-switch, so it is inert for every non-Vulkan core and reversible wholesale.
+
+### Vulkan side — `nanoarch_vulkan.c`
+- **Extension injection where the core owns the device.** `create_device_wrapper` now, when zero-copy
+  is armed, verifies `VK_KHR_external_memory_win32` + `VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32` via
+  `vkEnumerateDeviceExtensionProperties` and **appends them (dedup) to the core's own
+  `VkDeviceCreateInfo`** before calling `vkCreateDevice`. If either is unsupported (or the injected
+  create fails) it flips an internal fallback and creates the device **unmodified** — it never creates a
+  second device (spec §3 footgun).
+- **Exportable pool.** N slots of `VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM` (RGBA — **not** M1's BGRA; the GL zc path
+  ships RGBA and no channel swap belongs in the blit anymore), `TILING_OPTIMAL`,
+  `TRANSFER_DST | SAMPLED`, created with `VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo` (OPAQUE_WIN32) and
+  **dedicated allocations** (`VkMemoryDedicatedAllocateInfo` + `VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo`). Each
+  allocation's handle is exported via `vkGetMemoryWin32HandleKHR`.
+- **GL import** (in C, GL entry points resolved via opengl32/`wglGetProcAddress`, WGL context current):
+  `glCreateMemoryObjectsEXT` + `glImportMemoryWin32HandleEXT(OPAQUE_WIN32)` +
+  `glTexStorageMem2DEXT(GL_RGBA8, w, h, memObj, 0)`. The exported Win32 handle is `CloseHandle`d right
+  after import (GL takes its own reference — else one handle leaks per slot per realloc under the flip
+  rate; spec §3 footgun).
+- **Sync (spec §1.4).** Per-slot exportable Vk→GL "ready" semaphore
+  (`VkExportSemaphoreCreateInfo`/`vkGetSemaphoreWin32HandleKHR` ↔ `glImportSemaphoreWin32HandleEXT`).
+  Per frame the blit submit signals it; `glWaitSemaphoreEXT` (naming the slot's
+  `SHADER_READ_ONLY` layout) + `glFlush` order it into the GL share group before the encoder samples —
+  **layer 1**. A **layer-2** conservative mode (`CLOUD_GAME_VK_ZEROCOPY=fence`) additionally host-waits
+  the blit fence (still cheaper than M1's blit+copy+host-visibility chain) and is the A/B correctness
+  reference. Both modes signal the semaphore; the difference is only the extra host fence-wait.
+- **Per-frame flow** (`nano_vk_zc_frame`): acquire a released slot (free list, mutex-guarded; if none →
+  return 0 so the caller `OnDup`s — a drop beats a stall); barrier core→TRANSFER_SRC, slot
+  UNDEFINED→TRANSFER_DST, blit (LINEAR when scaling, NEAREST 1:1 — M1's F1 semantics), slot→SHADER_READ,
+  core back; submit under `lock_queue` signalling the ready semaphore + a per-slot fence; GL wait; return
+  the slot's GL texture id.
+- **Geometry flips (spec §1.6).** On extent change: `vkDeviceWaitIdle` → **retire** the current
+  generation (kept alive one flip so a texture GStreamer still holds is never freed under it — external
+  memory makes freeing-under-a-live-sampler a shared-memory use-after-free, worse than the GL path's
+  plain-texture case) → destroy the previously-retired generation → rebuild + re-export + re-import at
+  the new size. `zc_push` renegotiates the appsrc caps itself; the pool code does not touch the pipeline.
+  Fences + command buffers are geometry-independent and survive reallocs (created once).
+- **Teardown (spec §1.7).** GL imports/memory objects/semaphores die on the cothread (WGL context
+  current) BEFORE `nano_vk_predestroy` → the M1 order (context_destroy skip per hack → device →
+  instance) continues.
+- **Capability probe** `nano_vk_probe_zerocopy` — a throwaway instance (no device; enumeration needs
+  only a physical device) so the readback-vs-GL **pipeline decision is knowable at pipeline-BUILD time**
+  (the pipeline mode is chosen before the core's device exists). `CLOUD_GAME_VK_ZC_SIMULATE_NOEXT=1`
+  forces a negative to exercise the automatic fallback.
+
+### Go / config
+- `nanoarch.go`: per-room `Video.vk.zeroCopy` decision (staged by the coordinator, consumed+cleared in
+  `CoreLoad` like `HwContextOverride`); `setupVulkanZeroCopy` creates a **dedicated RGFW/WGL import
+  context** for the Vulkan room (thread.Main is inline on Windows, so the cothread IS the graphics
+  thread), wraps it for GStreamer via the existing `InitGLZeroCopy` unbind/share/rebind dance, then
+  builds the pool; `coreVideoRefresh`'s vk branch now emits a **GL texture** (`FrameInfo.Tex`, `Data`
+  nil) through the same path GL cores use, or `OnDup`s on a 0; teardown ordering (`GLContextGone` →
+  `nano_vk_zc_teardown` → import-context `Deinit`). `VulkanZeroCopySupported()` caches the probe.
+- `coordinatorhandlers.go`: **reverses the M1 guard** — the GL zero-copy pipeline (`m.GLZeroCopy`) now
+  arms for `gl-core || (vk-game && vkZeroCopySupported && !kill-switch)`. `CLOUD_GAME_VK_ZEROCOPY`:
+  `0`/`off` → M1 readback; `fence` → layer-2; anything else/unset → layer-1.
+- `graphics/zerocopy.go`: `ExternalRelease` hook so GStreamer's texture-release notify
+  (`goReleaseZeroCopyTexture` → `graphics.ReleaseZeroCopyTexture`) routes into the Vulkan pool's C free
+  list. GL cores leave it nil and use the existing GL pool unchanged.
+- Vendored `vulkan/vulkan_win32.h` verbatim from the LRPS2 tree (the Win32 external-memory/semaphore
+  entry points and structs).
+
+---
+
+## Acceptance criteria (spec §2)
+
+| # | Criterion | Status |
+|---|-----------|--------|
+| 1 | Hitching signature improves vs the 23:58:13 baseline (no 30–45 ms maxTick windows on the push path; audio 60/48000/forgiven=0) | **NOT VALIDATED** — needs a driven Stuntman session on the M2 binary (blocked: production-deploy gate) |
+| 2 | Visual correctness under MOTION (RGBA colours, no tearing/stale frames/marquee jitter, full high-res frame) | **NOT VALIDATED** — the spec-mandated moving-content test needs the deploy |
+| 3 | 448↔896 flips mid-session survive (pool realloc logs, caps reneg, no pipeline error) | **NOT VALIDATED** (realloc path implemented; unexercised live) |
