+## What was implemented (2 files, +70/−12)
+
+### 1. `overrides.go` — data-driven `WantsVulkanRenderer` (spec §1.1)
+Replaced the hard-coded `pcsx2_renderer` switch with a table keyed by option name → the set of values
+that mean "Vulkan room":
+```go
+var vulkanRendererOptions = map[string]map[string]struct{}{
+    "pcsx2_renderer":         {"paraLLEl-GS": {}, "Vulkan": {}},   // PS2 (M1+M2)
+    "mupen64plus-rdp-plugin": {"parallel": {}},                    // N64 paraLLEl-RDP (W2)
+}
+```
+`WantsVulkanRenderer` returns true iff any listed option is set to a listed value. `rdp-plugin=parallel`
+→ Vulkan room; `gliden64`/`angrylion` stay GL/software. W3/W4 cores (flycast/dolphin/ppsspp) join as
+single rows later — **not wired now** (spec §1.1). RSP selection (`rsp-plugin=parallel`) is an accuracy
+pairing the profile sets; the RENDERER selector is what decides the capture path.
+
+### 2. `nanoarch_vulkan.c` — v1 `create_device` zero-copy extension injection (spec §1.2/§1.3)
+The M2 zero-copy path needs `VK_KHR_external_memory_win32` + `VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32` on the
+core's VkDevice. For **v2** (paraLLEl-GS) that injection lives in `create_device_wrapper`. **v1 has no
+wrapper — the core calls `vkCreateDevice` itself** (libretro_vulkan.h: v1 `create_device` is deprecated
+precisely because it "cannot express … optional extensions" via a wrapper). The v1 mechanism to get
+extensions onto that device is the `required_device_extensions` argument — the core must enable whatever
+the frontend asks for. The old code passed `NULL, 0` there, so on a v1 core the zc extensions were never
+enabled and export would be silently invalid.
+
+W2 fix: in the v1 `create_device` branch, when zero-copy is armed and both extensions are supported
+(`vkEnumerateDeviceExtensionProperties`), pass them as `required_device_extensions`. If unsupported →
+set the readback fallback and ask for nothing. If `create_device` fails **with** the extensions → retry
+unmodified and run M1 readback (never a second device — spec §3 footgun). The bare self-created fallback
+device (core provides no `create_device` at all) also forces readback, since it carries neither the
+extensions nor a Vulkan renderer's required features.
+
+This is the **only** frontend change W2 needed. Everything else in the M1/M2 frontend (negotiation
+storage, interface v5, `set_image`/sync callbacks, the readback and zc frame paths, geometry realloc,
+teardown ordering) carries N64 unchanged, by design (M1 §8 / M2 kept the pool abstraction separable).
+`nano_vk_init` still runs on the LibCo cothread before `context_reset`; N64 (a LibCo core) uses the same
+same_thread machinery LRPS2 does.
