+## W3-readiness fix (post-review addendum, same branch): v1 headless instance lacked surface extensions
+
+**Evidence (reviewer's live probe on the SHIPPED binary — psp core, `hwContext: vulkan`):** the room
+armed vk, PPSSPP requested the Vulkan hw context, negotiation stored (`create_instance=no,
+create_device2=no` → v1 path), our frontend created the instance, then PPSSPP failed to bind and the
+worker **fastfailed 0xC0000409**:
+```
+[G3D] Failed to load VK instance function: vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceSupportKHR
+[G3D] Failed to load VK instance function: vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR
+[G3D] Failed to load VK instance function: vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceFormatsKHR
+[G3D] Failed to load VK instance function: vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfacePresentModesKHR
+```
+
+**Contract check (as tasked):** the vendored `libretro_vulkan.h` places no instance-extension
+obligation on a create_instance-less v1 frontend — the only surface language is in the `create_device`
+doc: "If surface is not VK_NULL_HANDLE, the instance from frontend will have been created with
+supported for VK_KHR_surface extension." We pass `VK_NULL_HANDLE` and never present, so the bare
+instance was contract-legal. But real cores are developed against RetroArch, whose instance always
+carries the surface extensions, and PPSSPP's VulkanContext loads the `vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurface*KHR`
+entry points **unconditionally** at instance-bind time — on our headless instance they resolved NULL.
+
+**Fix (`nanoarch_vulkan.c`, v1/fallback branch of `create_instance` only):** enable `VK_KHR_surface`
+(+ `VK_KHR_win32_surface`, which depends on it and is only added alongside it) when the loader
+advertises them — a global-level `vkEnumerateInstanceExtensionProperties` check (one of the three
+NULL-instance-resolvable functions), skipped silently if absent. Log line now reads
+`instance created by frontend (v1 path, N surface extension(s) enabled)`. No surface is ever created;
+no device-level change (PPSSPP never reached device creation; if it later wants `VK_KHR_swapchain`
+that is a follow-up with fresh evidence).
+
+**v2 path checked, unchanged:** in v2 the CORE authors the `VkInstanceCreateInfo` via
+`create_instance` and injects its own required instance extensions through our verbatim wrapper —
+paraLLEl-GS does exactly that and is proven live. The wrapper carries a comment noting the W3 fix is
+deliberately v1-only.
+
+**Blast radius:** the touched branch is the self-created-instance path, used by v1 cores
+(mupen64plus-next, PPSSPP) and the no-negotiation fallback. LRPS2/paraLLEl-GS (v2) does not execute
+it. Adding two loader-advertised instance extensions is additive for N64: mupen's own Vulkan loader
+tolerates (and under RetroArch expects) a surface-capable instance.
+
+**Proof:** in-place build exit 0 (`bin/worker.w2.exe`, 36,169,571 bytes); scratchpad patch
+regenerated (`fork.vulkan-w2.compile-proven.patch`, 2,237,299 bytes) → applies cleanly to pristine
+`13852a7` and builds from the patch alone (`worker-verify.exe`, byte-identical size; worktree
+removed). **No pool touches** — `worker.exe` still the shipped M2 binary; live validation of W2 + this
+fix happens together in the approved morning window (add a psp `hwContext: vulkan` probe to the
+runbook as arm 0/W3-smoke: expect the new log line and no 0xC0000409).
