+- **Live evidence (glworker-2, Crazy Taxi 1920×1440):** `[zc-stat] inflight=1/8 serials[X..X span=0]` (clean retention — NOT the Stuntman backlog class) with **`setimg_sem(waited=5006 none=13383→…)` — the `none` counter grows every frame, `waited` flat.** So **flycast passes ZERO set_image semaphores** (like paraLLEl-GS), so our copy has nothing to wait on.
+- **flycast source (`core/rend/vulkan/vk_context_lr.cpp`, `.h`):** `PresentFrame` → `endFrame` → `CommandPool::EndFrame` → `SubmitCommandBuffers(buffers, fence)` which does `queue.submit(SubmitInfo(nullptr,nullptr,buffers,**nullptr**), fence)` — **signals only a fence, NO signal semaphore** — then `set_image(handle, &img, **0, nullptr**, QueueFamilyIgnored)`. Same VkQueue as our copy (`vk.queue == ctx.queue`), and `SubmitCommandBuffers` DOES take our `lock_queue`/`unlock_queue` — so no concurrent-access validation error.
+- **The mechanism (why it's unlike paraLLEl-GS):** `rend.ThreadedRendering` **defaults enabled** (`shell/libretro/libretro.cpp:558`, `core/cfg/option.cpp:112`; option key `reicast_threaded_rendering`, values enabled/disabled). So flycast's GPU render is submitted **on a separate render thread**, while `video_cb`/our copy run on the emu cothread. `lock_queue` only *serializes* the two submits (prevents the validation error); it does **NOT order** flycast's render submit *before* our copy's blit. With no semaphore to encode the dependency, the copy races the render → reads pre/mid-render → garbage/stale. paraLLEl-GS is safe only because it is single-threaded (render→set_image→copy all sequential on one thread = deterministic order); flycast's threaded submit breaks exactly that ordering, and — unlike gc/Dolphin, which we patched to signal+pass a present semaphore (patch #3) — flycast provides none, so the cure our copy already implements has nothing to bind to.
+
+**dc fix design (two options; we own the flycast custom core):**
+- **Option B — config-only, cheapest test AND possible full fix (recommended first):** set `reicast_threaded_rendering: disabled` for dc/naomi/atomiswave. `retro_run` then calls `emu.render()` inline on the cothread → render submit → set_image → video_cb → our copy are all sequential on ONE thread = deterministic order = synced (identical safety to paraLLEl-GS). **Zero code, zero build, reversible via one config line.** If the garbage vanishes, the mechanism is 100% confirmed; keep it if dc holds 60fps (DC is light — likely fine), else move to Option A. flycast upstream flags threading "highly recommended" for perf, so measure fps.
+- **Option A — flycast custom-core patch #2, robust fix that KEEPS threading:** patch flycast to signal a VkSemaphore on the present-frame render submit and pass it to `set_image`: (1) add a `renderComplete` semaphore ring to `VulkanContext`; (2) add it as `signalSemaphores` on the present-pass `SubmitCommandBuffers` (the last submit before `set_image`, in `endFrame`/`CommandPool::EndFrame`); (3) `PresentFrame` passes `set_image(..., 1, &renderComplete[idx], queue_family)`. Our copy **already waits on set_image semaphores** (the gc semaphore-wait fix, `nanoarch_vulkan.c` ~1658) → it binds automatically → synced with threading intact. This mirrors the gc/Dolphin cure exactly; ~20 bounded lines in `vk_context_lr` + wiring the semaphore from `CommandPool::EndFrame` up to `PresentFrame`.
