+## The freeze, root-caused (the coordinator's rejection of my first "NO-GO" was correct)
+First attempt froze at the BIOS->game transition (~frame 147): `video_cb` delivered VALID frames with
+collapsed geometry (1400x4 / 560x2 — heights 2-4px), sub-16px-guarded to a dead stream (dupRatio=1). I
+initially wrote it off as "beetle-incompatible"; Eric rejected that (beetle is Themaister's reference
+client — the presumption is OUR interface). Reopened with instrument -> discriminate -> fix:
+
+- **Structural audit + instrumentation** (CLOUD_GAME_VK_DEBUG): beetle calls `get_sync_index` AND
+  `wait_sync_index` EVERY frame (299/300 ticks); every core that worked so far never calls them (the
+  "narrow subset" gap). Our v5 interface advanced `sync_index` ONLY in the readback path, and
+  `wait_sync_index` was a no-op. **Fixed both** (commits `35c757d`, `a6a5a24`) — real interface
+  completeness that benefits every future Vulkan core (sync index advances per frame in the zc path;
+  `wait_sync_index` now blocks on the real per-slot copy fence, the image-lifetime handshake
+  libretro_vulkan.h:405-412 promises). **These were necessary but NOT sufficient** — the geometry stayed
+  collapsed with them in.
+- **Transition trace** named it: frames 138-146 `64x64` (static), then frame 147 abrupt `1400x4` with a
+  fresh scanout handle each frame; NO `geometryChange`/SET_SYSTEM_AV_INFO. Source (beetle
+  `rhi/rhi_lib_vulkan.c:7104`): `display_height = last_scanline - initial_scanline + 1`. So the collapse
+  was in the visible-scanline window, not the sync protocol.
+- **Root cause = a bad core-options-v2 default** (the coordinator's cheapest hypothesis, #3). beetle's C
+  default for `last_scanline` is 239, but the core-options-v2 definition's first value token is **"210"**,
+  and the unset option resolved to a value that collapsed the range at the transition — the "values not
+  labels" / embedded-default class (dolphin patch 0016, pcsx frameskip). **Fix: pin the full scanline
+  window explicitly** (`initial_scanline:0 / last_scanline:239 / _pal:0/287 / crop_overscan:disabled`).
+  With that, frame 147 transitions `64x64 -> 1400x960` (full height) and the stream stays live.
+
+**Two-part fix**: the sync-index interface completeness (fork, shippable, all cores) + the scanline-option
+pin (config, load-bearing — the block header marks it DO-NOT-REMOVE). Save path: `.srm` via
+RETRO_MEMORY_SAVE_RAM (memcard1 enabled); pcsx test saves were quarantine-renamed then restored on the
+earlier revert, now beetle writes its own (continuity waived).
+
